        text: 'Vantage is brought in by a regional director at a grid operator. Three projects started separately in her region: a readiness check for planned jobs (team A), a new materials-kit process (team B) and a planning-tool upgrade (IT). All three report green. Cancellations are still at 14%; her target is 8%. The readiness check reads material data that team B is redesigning, and the IT release in Q3 changes the field the readiness check uses.\n\nWhat you do: make it a programme with one number, cancellations from 14% to 8%. Put the dependencies on one page: the material-data definition, the tool field change, and the planners all three teams need. Team B owns the material-data definition and freezes it by week 6; IT tests its Q3 release against the readiness check before go-live, the day it goes into use. A monthly programme board with her, the three project owners and the planning manager reports the outcome number, with an estimate of what each project contributes.',
