        kind: 'worked',
        text: 'A metal parts manufacturer with three plants starts an ERP programme: budget €2.4M, 24 months. Merijn helps set it up.\n\nVision statement, one sentence for the shop floor: “Every order planned in one system, with live stock, in all three plants.” Target operating model: weekly planning in the system, buyers ordering on system proposals, one item master (the central list of all parts and materials). Tranches: 1, finance and purchasing in plant A (months 1–9, €900k); 2, planning and production in plant A (months 10–16); 3, plants B and C (months 17–24).\n\nRoles: the COO is SRO, an experienced IT project director is programme manager, and in each plant the operations manager is business change manager. Tranche 1 is expected to save €300k a year from month 9 on, through less manual invoice checking and fewer rush orders. By month 24 that is 15 months × €25k = €375k already earned, before the programme ends.',
