        text: 'An ERP programme at a metal plant goes live in eight weeks and reports green. The PMO tracks milestones only. In the second data-migration test, 18% of the item master records (the central list of parts and materials) failed the quality check.\n\nThe programme manager says it will be fixed by the cutover, the weekend the old system is switched off. Users have had half the planned training. The SRO asks Merijn, who is not part of the programme, what he thinks.',
        ask: 'What would you propose to the SRO?',
        reveal: 'Propose an independent go-live readiness check in the next two weeks: three days, by someone outside the programme, for example the IT manager of a sister plant with an external reviewer. Agree the criteria first: at most a set share of failing records, users trained, a rehearsed cutover, and support ready on the floor.\n\nThe reviewers rate readiness and give three to five recommendations. The SRO then decides go, go with conditions, or move the date. Ask the PMO to report the data-quality figure weekly from now on, not just milestones.',
